# ─── Production (docker compose) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` next to docker-compose.yml on the server. See docs/DEPLOY.md.

# The public hostname. Its DNS A/AAAA record must point at this server before
# the first `docker compose up`, or Caddy cannot obtain the TLS certificate.
DOMAIN=resume.example.com

# Let's Encrypt contacts this address about certificate problems.
ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Optional tuning. Defaults suit a 2 vCPU / 4 GB VPS.
# Exports rendered at the same time. Each needs ~250 MB of RAM.
# PDF_CONCURRENCY=2
# Exports one IP address may request per minute.
# PDF_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=30
# How long an export may wait for a free slot before the user is told to retry.
# PDF_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# Longest a single render may take.
# PDF_RENDER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Hard memory cap for the pdf container.
# PDF_MEMORY_LIMIT=1536m


# ─── Local development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing is required. `npm run dev` proxies /api/pdf to a pdf-service on
# http://localhost:3040 (see vite.config.ts); start one with:
#   cd pdf-service && RENDER_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173 npm start
#
# Only to point the app at a PDF service on a different origin, put this in
# `.env.local` (Vite reads VITE_-prefixed variables at build time):
# VITE_PDF_SERVICE_URL=https://pdf.example.com
# That service must then list the app's origin in its ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
